- 2026-10-24 09:15 UTC: build step 4, part B2 (branch `feat/117-b2-reviews`): item reviews with memory, and the end rules. A review is due at a digest after the minimum when every question has a card, no review waits and an item has no standing decision; its marker is `items:` with each card's version and the required hypotheses, so none is asked when nothing changed. The package holds every card with its cited claims (quotes cut to 400 characters), rubric and standing decision, the required hypotheses, `decide`, the figures and the criteria, and is shortened from the items that stand first, said. Each reviewer, in parallel, answers each item to decide (`answered` with a certainty, `insufficient` with next experiments, `open` with gaps; `supported`, `refuted`, `undecided`); code checks each; the majority decides, with the median certainty and the dissent kept (`review_item`, `item_decision`; events `review_items`, `item_decided`, and `review_panel` with `decided` and `open`). The workers' gaps come from the standing open decisions only. A pass closes the run with `every question is answered` after its paper; the progress rule (`research_progress` at each digest, `research_stopped`) closes it with `PROGRESS_STOPPED` after its paper, whose package says which questions stayed open. Decided in the build: the majority is the verdict more of the passing reviewers gave than any other, and a tie for the most is open (undecided); with an even count the median certainty is the lower of the two in the middle; a hypothesis's decision, `undecided` included, stands for good; the progress rule waits while a review waits and never ends a run whose items all have ends (that run waits for the pass or the owner's word); an owner's rejection keeps the decisions, asked again when a card changes; a run that ended takes no new card, so its decisions stay as they were for its paper. Not yet: the Reviews tab and the History lines of the new events (part C2), and the paper written from the cards (part C1).
- 2026-10-24 09:18 UTC: build step 6, part C2 (branch `feat/117-c2-dashboard`): control reads a research run's items from its events (`hypothesis_status`, `review_items`, `item_decided`, `review_panel`'s `decided` and `open`, `research_progress`, and each task's `question` and `yield`) and `get_run` and `run_queue` carry them (`hypotheses`, `decisions`, `standing`, `progress`, each review's times, items and decisions). The run's Overview shows each question with its card, the decision that stands, its gaps, its share of the last 20 tasks, its yield and saturation, and the progress rule; the Reviews tab (goal 116) on the run's and the campaign's page; a Hypotheses tab with the owner's Promote, Return to pool and Retire, which send the new owner command `hypothesis_status` (its kind is in `src/core/commands.ts`; the harness's handling of it is part B1's); the Experiments tab shows each task's question and yield. Not yet: the planner's state on the run's page (part B1's model planner), and the harness's events from parts B1 and B2, which control reads in the build design's shapes.
